cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "GovMembersTN: Members of Tunisian Governments, 1861-2026"
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Hammami
    given-names: Mohamed Dhia
repository-code: "https://github.com/MedDhia/GovMembersTN"
abstract: >-
  An individual-level dataset of members of Tunisian governments from the
  beylical period to the present, covering 884 people and 3,151 ministerial
  appointments across 57 cabinets and 23 government spells. Each appointment
  carries a harmonised portfolio, a cabinet rank, dated tenure bounds with
  recorded precision, and where available a Journal Officiel decree citation.
  Person-level variables cover birth date and place coded to governorate and
  region, gender, education, party affiliation and profession. Four network
  layers are published alongside the tables: bipartite person-cabinet
  affiliation, time-aware co-membership weighted by days of overlapping
  service, directed within-portfolio succession, and typed homophily ties.
  Built from Wikidata, French and Arabic Wikipedia, the Tunisian Journal
  Officiel, rulers.org and the Tunisian press, with entity resolution across
  Latin and Arabic scripts.
keywords:
  - Tunisia
  - political elites
  - cabinet ministers
  - authoritarianism
  - regime change
  - Middle East and North Africa
  - social network analysis
  - prosopography
license: MIT
